TEXT: We need digits \(a<b<c<d\), each 1–9, sum 20.  
Let \(x_1=a\), \(x_2=b-a\), \(x_3=c-b\), \(x_4=d-c\), \(x_5=9-d\) (all ≥1 except possibly \(x_5\ge0\)).  
Sum condition: \(a+b+c+d=20\).  
In terms of \(x_i\): \(a=x_1\), \(b=x_1+x_2\), \(c=x_1+x_2+x_3\), \(d=x_1+x_2+x_3+x_4\).  
Sum = \(4x_1+3x_2+2x_3+x_4=20\).  
